[% META
        title = "Authentication Evolution Plan  -  Comserv"
   description = "Authoritative plan for Comserv authentication and credential architecture. Defines the session-compatibility contract templates depend on, and owns the credential-storage defect (per-table credentials in JSON files) that blocks automated container propagation. Tracked as project 243 (AUTH-EVO) under 201 SECURITY."
   roles = "admin,developer"
   TemplateType = "Documentation"
   category = "security,authentication,credentials,architecture"
   page_version = "2.00"
   last_updated = "Fri Aug 07 2026"
   site_specific = "false"
   project_id = "243"
   project_code = "AUTH-EVO"
%]
[% PageVersion = 'Documentation/AuthenticationEvolutionPlan.tt,v 2.00 2026/08/07 hermes-agent Exp shanta - Converted raw markdown to template-compliant .tt (RULE P3); linked project 243 (RULE P1); added AUTH-R1..R4 dependency register and routine re-audit (RULE P2)' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %]
    [% PageVersion %]
[% END %]

<div class="container">
    <h1 style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">Authentication Evolution Plan</h1>

    <div class="last-updated" style="color: var(--text-muted-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">
        Last Updated: 2026-08-07 |
        Version: 2.00 |
        Project: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=243" style="color: var(--link-color);">#243 (AUTH-EVO)</a> |
        Status: ACTIVE
    </div>

    <div class="warning" style="background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-left: 4px solid var(--warning-color); padding: var(--spacing-medium); border-radius: 4px; margin: var(--spacing-medium) 0;">
        <strong style="color: var(--warning-color);">ACTIVE &mdash; DO NOT CHANGE WITHOUT EXPLICIT PERMISSION.</strong>
        <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); margin: var(--spacing-small) 0 0 0;">This document exists to stop the authentication approach being reinvented every session. Any change to authentication strategy must update this document <em>and</em> get explicit approval. Other plans (notably <a href="/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN" style="color: var(--link-color);">the Availability &amp; Load Balancing Master Plan</a>) may <strong>raise requirements</strong> here, but must not redesign authentication themselves.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- TABLE OF CONTENTS -->
    <div id="toc" class="row" style="margin: var(--spacing-large) 0; background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.15); padding: var(--spacing-medium); border-left: 4px solid var(--primary-color); border-radius: 4px;">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); margin-top: 0;">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--text-muted-color); font-family: var(--body-font); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">Jump to section:</p>
            <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--spacing-small);">
                <a href="#overview" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">1. Overview</a>
                <a href="#current-state" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">2. Current State</a>
                <a href="#root-defect" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">3. Root Defect</a>
                <a href="#credential-sources" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">4. Credential Sources</a>
                <a href="#phases" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">5. Evolution Phases</a>
                <a href="#requirements" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">6. Requirements Raised</a>
                <a href="#rules" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">7. Implementation Rules</a>
                <a href="#project-tracking" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">Project Tracking</a>
                <a href="#see-also" style="color: var(--nav-text); text-decoration: none; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 3px; background-color: var(--nav-bg); display: inline-block;">See Also</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. OVERVIEW -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">1. Overview</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">This document defines the authentication and credential strategy for Comserv, to maintain session-to-session consistency and prevent the approach being reinvented. It covers two related concerns: <strong>how users authenticate</strong> (sessions, roles, templates) and <strong>where service credentials live</strong> (database, SSH, registry, API tokens).</p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">Scope boundary: this plan <em>owns</em> the authentication and credential architecture. Infrastructure plans consume it and may raise requirements against it (&sect;6), but must not implement authentication changes themselves.</p>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">&uarr; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. CURRENT STATE -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="current-state" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">2. Current State</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);"><strong>Problem:</strong> authentication broke in the menu system branch when the Catalyst authentication framework was introduced while templates expected simple session-based auth.</p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);"><strong>Root cause:</strong> templates (<code>.tt</code> files) are the application documentation, and they expect:</p>
            <ul style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li><code>c.session.username</code></li>
                <li><code>c.session.roles</code> (as an array)</li>
                <li>Simple session checks</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">This session contract is <strong>binding</strong>: any authentication change must continue to populate it, or templates break site-wide.</p>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">&uarr; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3. ROOT DEFECT -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="root-defect" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">3. The root credential defect</h2>
            <div style="background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-left: 4px solid var(--caution-color); padding: var(--spacing-medium); border-radius: 4px; margin: var(--spacing-small) 0;">
                <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); margin: 0;">The credential problem was created <strong>at the very beginning of the process</strong>: the assumption that <strong>each table needed its own credential</strong>, and that those credentials belonged in JSON files.</p>
            </div>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">Consequences that are now blocking other work:</p>
            <ul style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li>Secrets multiply per node and per rotation, so credential handling does not scale to multiple hosts.</li>
                <li>Automated container propagation is impossible if a human must hand-place credential files on each node.</li>
                <li>Observed 2026-08-07: <code>~/.comserv/secrets/dbi/</code> holds <strong>16 connection files</strong>, several stale (<code>backup_*</code>, <code>zerotier_*</code>, <code>sqlite_*</code>). These must be audited, not lifted wholesale into a new store.</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">&uarr; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. CREDENTIAL SOURCES -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="credential-sources" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">4. Credential sources as implemented today</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">Verified 2026-08-07 by reading <code>lib/Comserv/Model/RemoteDB.pm</code> <code>_load_config()</code>. It tries sources in order and stops at the first that yields config:</p>
            <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: var(--spacing-medium) 0;">
                <tr>
                    <th style="background-color: var(--table-header-bg); color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Order</th>
                    <th style="background-color: var(--table-header-bg); color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Source</th>
                    <th style="background-color: var(--table-header-bg); color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Mechanism</th>
                    <th style="background-color: var(--table-header-bg); color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Status in code</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">1</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Mounted secret files</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);"><code>_load_from_k8s_secrets()</code> scans <code>&lt;base&gt;/dbi/*.json</code> across six paths, including <code>~/.comserv/secrets</code> and <code>/var/run/secrets/comserv/</code></td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Preferred</td>
                </tr>
                <tr style="background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.12);">
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">2</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Environment variables</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);"><code>COMSERV_DB_&lt;CONN&gt;_&lt;FIELD&gt;</code></td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Supported fallback</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">3</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);"><code>db_config.json</code></td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);"><code>_find_db_config_file()</code>, six search paths</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);"><strong>DEPRECATED</strong> &mdash; the code logs "MIGRATE TO K8S SECRETS"</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">The mechanism therefore already exists and already expresses a preference. The real problem is that <strong>all three are live at once</strong>, so nobody can say which source a given host is actually using. Deciding the end state is this project's work &mdash; not the infrastructure plan's.</p>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">&uarr; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 5. PHASES -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="phases" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">5. Evolution phases</h2>

            <h3 id="phase-1" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); font-size: var(--font-size-large);">5.1 Phase 1 &mdash; Menu system branch (CURRENT)</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);"><strong>Goal:</strong> fix authentication so menu development can continue. <strong>Approach:</strong> hybrid compatibility layer.</p>
            <ul style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li>Keep the Catalyst authentication framework in the controller.</li>
                <li>Populate session variables for template compatibility.</li>
                <li>Document as "transition architecture".</li>
            </ul>
            <div style="background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.15); padding: var(--spacing-medium); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 4px; margin: var(--spacing-small) 0;">
                <pre style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: monospace; margin: 0;"><code># In User.pm controller after successful $c-&gt;authenticate()
$c-&gt;session-&gt;{username} = $user-&gt;username;
$c-&gt;session-&gt;{user_id}  = $user-&gt;id;
$c-&gt;session-&gt;{roles}    = $user-&gt;roles; # properly formatted array</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);"><strong>Files to modify:</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/User.pm</code> only. <strong>Templates:</strong> NO CHANGES.</p>

            <h3 id="phase-2" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); font-size: var(--font-size-large);">5.2 Phase 2 &mdash; Security branch (FUTURE)</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);"><strong>Goal:</strong> complete modern authentication system, with full Catalyst auth and template migration. Scope: a dedicated branch.</p>

            <h3 id="phase-3" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); font-size: var(--font-size-large);">5.3 Phase 3 &mdash; Credential consolidation (NEW, 2026-08-07)</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">Added because infrastructure work is now blocked by the credential design. Retires the per-table credential assumption (&sect;3), settles the source-of-truth question (&sect;4), and extends the policy to non-DB credentials (SSH, registry, API tokens). Tracked as <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo') %]?project_id=243" style="color: var(--link-color);">todos under project #243</a>.</p>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">&uarr; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 6. REQUIREMENTS RAISED -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="requirements" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">6. Requirements raised by other plans</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">Other plans state what they need from authentication and raise a todo here. They do <strong>not</strong> implement the change themselves. A requirement below may <strong>block</strong> the raising plan, and that is the correct outcome &mdash; better than two plans redesigning the same subsystem in different directions.</p>
            <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: var(--spacing-medium) 0;">
                <tr>
                    <th style="background-color: var(--table-header-bg); color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Req</th>
                    <th style="background-color: var(--table-header-bg); color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Requirement</th>
                    <th style="background-color: var(--table-header-bg); color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Todo</th>
                    <th style="background-color: var(--table-header-bg); color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Blocks</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">AUTH-R1</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Credentials must reach a pod without hand-placing files on each node</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=1965" style="color: var(--link-color);">#1965</a></td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">INFRA-HA Phase C / G</td>
                </tr>
                <tr style="background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.12);">
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">AUTH-R2</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Sessions valid across BOTH app replicas</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=1966" style="color: var(--link-color);">#1966</a></td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">INFRA-HA Phase D</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">AUTH-R3</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">One credential set per <em>connection</em>, not per table</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=1967" style="color: var(--link-color);">#1967</a></td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">INFRA-HA Phase G</td>
                </tr>
                <tr style="background-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.12);">
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">AUTH-R4</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Managed credentials for .198 and any new node</td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=1968" style="color: var(--link-color);">#1968</a></td>
                    <td style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font); padding: var(--spacing-small); border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">INFRA-HA Phase F &mdash; <strong>already blocking</strong></td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">AUTH-R4 is not hypothetical: on 2026-08-07 the .198 replica assessment could not be performed because its SSH credentials differ from .126 and are held in no managed store.</p>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">&uarr; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 7. RULES -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="rules" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">7. Implementation rules</h2>
            <h3 id="rules-ai" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); font-size: var(--font-size-large);">7.1 For AI sessions</h3>
            <ol style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li><strong>READ THIS DOCUMENT FIRST</strong> before making any authentication change.</li>
                <li><strong>Phase 1 only</strong> &mdash; implement the compatibility layer; do NOT change templates.</li>
                <li><strong>No DBEncy references</strong> &mdash; use the existing working database models.</li>
                <li><strong>ASK PERMISSION</strong> before changing the authentication approach.</li>
                <li><strong>UPDATE THIS DOCUMENT</strong> when making approved changes.</li>
                <li><strong>Do not solve auth inside another plan.</strong> Raise a requirement here (&sect;6) instead.</li>
            </ol>
            <h3 id="rules-dev" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); font-size: var(--font-size-large);">7.2 For developers</h3>
            <ul style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li>The authentication approach is documented here; changes require updating this document.</li>
                <li>Templates are documentation &mdash; changing them requires the Phase 2 branch.</li>
                <li>Controllers must use existing database models, populate session variables, and keep template compatibility.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3 id="success" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font); font-size: var(--font-size-large);">7.3 Phase 1 success criteria</h3>
            <ul style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                <li>Login works with username/password</li>
                <li>Session variables populated correctly</li>
                <li>Templates display user info properly</li>
                <li>Role-based access works</li>
                <li>Logout clears session appropriately</li>
                <li>Menu system development can continue</li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align: right; margin-top: var(--spacing-small);"><a href="#toc" style="color: var(--link-color); font-size: var(--font-size-small);">&uarr; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PROJECT TRACKING (RULE P1) -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="project-tracking" style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--header-font);">Project Tracking</h2>
            <p style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
                Owning project: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=243" style="color: var(--link-color);">#243 (AUTH-EVO) Authentication &amp; Credential Architecture</a>
                &mdash; sub-project of <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=201" style="color: var(--link-color);">#201 SECURITY</a>,
                sibling of <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=239" style="color: var(--link-color);">#239 IMGSEC</a> (credentials leaking into image layers).
            </p>
            <ul style="color: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--body-font);">
